.TH nmond 1 "2026-04-09" "0.2.0" "nmond man page"
.SH NAME
nmond \- Ncurses based System Performance Monitor for Darwin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nmond
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nmond
is an interactive, ncurses-based system performance monitor for Darwin (macOS).
It displays CPU utilization, memory and swap usage, disk I/O, network traffic,
GPU metrics, energy statistics, and top processes in a terminal interface.
.PP
Press
.B h
while running to see a list of interactive key commands.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.B c / C
CPU load / CPU long-term graph
.TP
.B d / D
Disk I/O / Disk I/O long-term graph
.TP
.B e
Energy statistics
.TP
.B g
GPU metrics
.TP
.B h, H, ?
Help screen
.TP
.B i
System information (hardware and kernel)
.TP
.B m
Memory and Swap
.TP
.B n / N
Network / Network long-term graph
.TP
.B t / T
Top processes by CPU / Top with command arguments
.TP
.B r / R
Top processes by memory / Top by memory with command arguments
.TP
.B b
Toggle black & white mode
.TP
.B + / \-
Increase / decrease refresh rate
.TP
.B Up / Down
Scroll display
.TP
.B q
Quit
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NMOND
A string of key characters to activate panels on startup (e.g., NMOND="cdm").
.TP
.B NMON
Compatibility alias for NMOND with key translation from the original nmon.
.TP
.B NMONDEBUG
If set, enables debug mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR vm_stat (1),
.BR iostat (8)
